<https://ontology.local/support#Escalation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.local/support#Escalation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Escalation" .
<https://ontology.local/support#Escalation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Escalation" .
<https://ontology.local/support#Escalation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The act of a support agent referring a ticket to development because it has been identified as a defect or as a request for new functionality. The Escalation produces a Jira issue and is the only legitimate way a Jira ID becomes associated with a ticket." .
<https://ontology.local/support#Escalation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The act of a support agent referring a ticket to development because it has been identified as a defect or as a request for new functionality. The Escalation produces a Jira issue and is the only legitimate way a Jira ID becomes associated with a ticket." .
<https://ontology.local/support#Escalation> <https://ontology.local/support#domainType> "Support" .
<https://ontology.local/support#Escalation> <https://ontology.local/support#status> "Canonical" .
<https://ontology.local/support#Escalation> <https://ontology.local/support#identityRule> "Surrogate: generated UUID. There is no natural key — the same ticket can be escalated more than once, and the same Jira issue can receive escalations from many tickets." .
