<https://ontology.local/support#SupportEntitlement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.local/support#SupportEntitlement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SupportEntitlement" .
<https://ontology.local/support#SupportEntitlement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "SupportEntitlement" .
<https://ontology.local/support#SupportEntitlement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The tier of support service an account is entitled to receive. The tier governs response time targets, escalation rights and channel access. Entitlement is a property of the account, not of an individual ticket or license." .
<https://ontology.local/support#SupportEntitlement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The tier of support service an account is entitled to receive. The tier governs response time targets, escalation rights and channel access. Entitlement is a property of the account, not of an individual ticket or license." .
<https://ontology.local/support#SupportEntitlement> <https://ontology.local/support#domainType> "Customer" .
<https://ontology.local/support#SupportEntitlement> <https://ontology.local/support#status> "Canonical" .
<https://ontology.local/support#SupportEntitlement> <https://ontology.local/support#identityRule> "Natural key: the canonical tier code (`STANDARD`, `PREMIUM`). Entitlement is a controlled vocabulary, not a per-account record — the per-account fact is the `hasEntitlement` link, and its effective dates live on the link." .
