<https://ontology.local/support#Ticket> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.local/support#Ticket> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ticket" .
<https://ontology.local/support#Ticket> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Ticket" .
<https://ontology.local/support#Ticket> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A single recorded request for support from a customer account, tracked from submission to resolution. One ticket represents one customer problem. It is owned by exactly one account, assigned to at most one agent at a time, carries exactly one severity, is governed by exactly one SLA, and may be escalated to development. It may be submitted by a Contact at the account or, where the customer buys through one, by a Partner acting on the account's behalf." .
<https://ontology.local/support#Ticket> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A single recorded request for support from a customer account, tracked from submission to resolution. One ticket represents one customer problem. It is owned by exactly one account, assigned to at most one agent at a time, carries exactly one severity, is governed by exactly one SLA, and may be escalated to development. It may be submitted by a Contact at the account or, where the customer buys through one, by a Partner acting on the account's behalf." .
<https://ontology.local/support#Ticket> <https://ontology.local/support#domainType> "Support" .
<https://ontology.local/support#Ticket> <https://ontology.local/support#status> "Canonical" .
<https://ontology.local/support#Ticket> <https://ontology.local/support#identityRule> "The CRM ticket/case number is authoritative. Ticket numbers are unique within a CRM but not across CRMs — a fully qualified ticket identity is `systemCode` + `ticketNumber`. This is a real collision risk in reporting." .
<https://ontology.local/support#Ticket> <https://ontology.local/support#sourceFile> "Ontology/Entities/Ticket.md" .
